## Colour roles in Home Assistant

<h3 id="bg-col-02">Choose a colour by its job</h3>

The theme colour marks navigation and actions. Text colours are for reading. Focus and error colours mark an interaction state. Device colours show a native device state. Chart colours name a source.

The Red theme colour is the same as the error colour (`#CA3535`<%= copy_hex.('#CA3535', 'the error colour in light mode') %> in light mode and `#F0C6C6`<%= copy_hex.('#F0C6C6', 'the error colour in dark mode') %> in dark mode). The Green theme colour is the same as the success colour (`#0F7A52`<%= copy_hex.('#0F7A52', 'the success colour in light mode') %> in light mode and `#BCDACF`<%= copy_hex.('#BCDACF', 'the success colour in dark mode') %> in dark mode). With either theme, say an error or success in words, as [Test combinations and keep another cue](colour.html#bg-col-03) explains. Choose a status fill and its text colour together. A dark-mode error text colour is not always a safe button background.

This example shows 3 entities on a dashboard card. Each state is written out, so none depends on colour. Unavailable is not shown as 0°C.

<%= example('bg-colour-state-labels') %>

<h3 id="bg-col-04">Separate dividers from editable boundaries</h3>

Use `civica-border-quiet` for dividers and quiet card edges. Use `civica-border-interactive` for controls people need to find, and `civica-input-border` for text fields. Keep the strong input and focus styles.

Group content with headings and spacing, not black outlines. Do not lighten every border either: a text field, a focus ring and a card edge do different jobs. Keep native circle and pill shapes where they carry meaning, as on a switch, badge or gauge.

This example shows the field for renaming an area. The card edge is quiet. The text field has a strong border and, when selected, a clear focus ring.

<%= example('bg-colour-boundaries') %>

<h3 id="bg-col-05">Keep device, warning and notification meaning</h3>

Keep the native icon and state colours for a device, and keep its name and state readable. An unavailable sensor is not a zero reading or a device that is off. A manufacturer's logo is content, not part of the interface's identity.

The [notification badge](../components/notification-badge.html) keeps its fixed colour and shape with every theme colour. Its count is not an alarm level, and a coloured dot does not replace a warning message. Give success, a pending action and a failure their own wording as well as their own look.
